@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Web Worker backend contracts — stage two
+
+Baseline: Bend 2.0.27, `d37909174ebd664338ae3194799a9e0899dedd51`.
+These are downstream implementation contracts. They do not extend Bend's value
+theory or prove correctness of browser threads.
+
+| Contract | Implementation and tested boundary |
+| --- | --- |
+| Legacy preservation | Separate worker compiler/API. No-directive JS and native-C outputs retain baseline pins. A 639-file differential lane compares parse/check outcomes and compile-fixture JS/C hashes. New web policies are ignored by native output; legacy public JS warns or rejects require by selected enforcement. |
+| Value preservation | Coarse helpers invoke original synchronous generated functions, or a synchronous policy interpreter around those functions. Joins preserve source binding order and arithmetic trees. Independent integer/image expectations and same-engine serial/worker comparisons are covered. Production module/browser acceptance remains open. |
+| Erasure and theory | Scheduling metadata is absent from equality/typing decisions. Existing liveness/saturation helpers exclude dead work. Ref conversion/template copies preserve policy where live. A checked equality between required and never-marked calls is tested; the formal core is unchanged. |
+| Task legality | Require/force never bypass first-order schema, closed named-call, effect, unsafe, callback, size, protocol or capacity checks. Continuation-held local closures/Arrays do not become transportable. |
+| Arguments and dynamic scope | Arguments finish in the caller's context, then the callee region begins. Argument helper execution cannot witness that callee's requirement. Context belongs to invocation/frame records, not a mutable process flag. |
+| Require witness | At least one actual task belonging to a non-waived required region completes on a helper. Nested helper requirements coalesce. Conditional witness-free paths may trigger one explicitly logged whole-call dispatch; no dummy ping or unrelated task counts. |
+| Never | No dispatch originates inside its dynamic extent, including nested bang/auto work. It stays in the current executor. An ancestor containing an island may be remote. Require below never conflicts; strict rejects, permissive warns and keeps never. |
+| Caps and isolation | Source/enclosing/session caps take their minimum and bound distinct participating helpers. Concurrent roots retain separate region/witness sets but share one bounded pool. A smaller session can honor a larger cap with one helper. |
+| Strict/permissive failure | Static unsupported/disabled require has compiler diagnostics. Runtime unavailable/budget/nonfinite/conflict cases reject or record a local waiver. Actual computation/protocol failures always fail publication; they are not retried as capability fallback. |
+| Snapshot stability | Supported host graphs are copied before first suspension; no surprising freeze/detach or caller-object identity cache. Invalid shapes reject. Unsupported public signatures use the original wholly synchronous compatibility route, not an unsafe asynchronous borrowed graph. |
+| Transport | Clone is default. Optional typed packed buffers use only runtime-owned transferables, bounded iterative encoding/decoding and explicit graph references. DAG sharing is message-local; managed residency/cross-message identity is not claimed. |
+| Numeric boundary | Finite F32 task inputs/outputs and signed zero are covered. Bit-sensitive internal paths remain ineligible even behind integer signatures. Nonfinite host values select local/required enforcement; remote nonfinite output fails visibly. No NaN payload, cross-engine or native bit-equivalence claim. |
+| Async containment | Generator/frame coordination is separate from serial functions and tail trampolines. Promises are scheduling/API objects, not constructor fields or intrinsic operands. Higher-order policy-bearing runtime closures are conservatively rejected in strict worker output. |
+| Bounded adaptive work | Existing parallel lets only. Profile count/history, frontier depth/expansions, region depth/count, jobs, queues and accepted data are bounded. Unknown/unstable work stays local; profiles learn only from real executions and reset with the session/build. |
+| Ordered failure-free joins | Prepared siblings bind results by source slot, never arrival order. No successful partial root is published. Reply validation precedes releasing job records. |
+| Protocol isolation | Content-bound build/schema identity, protocol, epoch, invocation, fork, slot, function and job binding. Allowlisted numeric functions only; no eval/source transport. Malformed, duplicate, stale or wrong-build/slot replies cannot satisfy a pending root. |
+| Lifecycle | Cancellation invalidates roots and queued jobs; busy helper replies remain inert. Close releases listeners/references and terminates owned workers. No unbounded restart/retry loop; cancellation alone cannot preempt synchronous helper code. |
+| Measurement honesty | Full invocation timing includes accepted snapshots, packing/clone, receiver reconstruction, scheduling and joins. Raw paired positive/negative samples and load shifts are retained. Scheduler byte counters are not hard process-memory limits; Node/classic-worker results are not production static-module performance. |
+
+## Trusted-value optimization boundary
+
+`measureTrusted` is an internal bounded sizing pass for generated values and
+accepted invocation snapshots. It avoids repeatedly building host property
+metadata for objects whose representation the compiler already owns. It retains
+schema/primitive/F32, size, string and graph checks. It must **not** replace
+`snapshotArgs` on arbitrary host inputs or raw cloned worker replies. Packed
+reconstruction performs validation and accounting while decoding rather than
+walking the result again. Tests compare packed accounting with the public scan.
+
+## Operational policies are not values
+
+A strict requirement failure rejects the asynchronous backend invocation. It
+does not produce a new Bend constructor or alter pure equality. Parser syntax
+errors are errors under every policy. Native `!` and web metadata are separate;
+`Carb.bangs`, native `flat_of`, and C layouts do not stand in for dynamic region,
+suspension or wire-schema analysis.
+
+## Remaining acceptance boundary
+
+Passing local tests is not all of the supplied guide's exit criteria. Actual
+production module-worker static hosting, CSP/MIME/offline failure routes,
+release/HTML bundling, multiple browser engines and browser/device performance
+remain unverified here. Large cheap immutable inputs still have material public
+snapshot overhead. Do not label these gaps as passed, infer general speedup, or
+claim hard allocation limits for worker task bodies.
